{"source_id":"arXiv:math/0508143","title":"\\LargeVerma modules for Yangians","abstract":"We study the Verma modules M(mu(u)) over the Yangian Y(a) associated with a simple Lie algebra a. We give necessary and sufficient conditions for irreducibility of M(mu(u)). Moreover, regarding the simple quotient L(mu(u)) of M(mu(u)) as an a-module, we give necessary and sufficient conditions for finite-dimensionality of the weight subspaces of L(mu(u)).","authors":["Y. Billig","V. Futorny","A. Molev"],"year":"2005","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0508143","doi":"10.48550/arXiv.math/0508143","cluster":"quantum_algebra","cards":[{"card_id":"ma-c-602a981ec6ababd1bf6d","label":"Abstract","kind":"abstract","line":157,"snippet":"We study the Verma modules $M(\\mu(u))$ over the Yangian $\\Y(\\agot)$ associated with a simple Lie algebra $\\agot$. We give necessary and sufficient conditions for irreducibility of $M(\\mu(u))$. …"},{"card_id":"ma-c-d50593c910baa77c274e","label":"Equation ef","kind":"equation","line":299,"snippet":"[h_i^{(r)},h_j^{(s)}]=0, [e_i^{(r)},f_j^{(s)}]=\\delta_{ij}h_i^{(r+s)}, [h_i^{(0)},e_j^{(s)}]=d_i\\tss a_{ij}e_j^{(s)}, [h_i^{(0)},f_j^{(s)}]=-d_i\\tss a_{ij}f_j^{(s)},\\non [h_i^{(r+1)},e_j^{(s)}] …"}],"conclusions_only":false,"held":2,"macros":{"non":"\\nonumber","scl":"\\scriptstyle","wt":"\\widetilde","wh":"\\widehat","ot":"\\otimes","fand":"\\quad\\text{and}\\quad","Fand":"\\qquad\\text{and}\\qquad","ts":"\\,","tss":"\\hspace{1pt}","tpr":"t^{\\tss\\prime}","spr":"s^{\\tss\\prime}","U":"{\\rm U}","Z":"{\\rm Z}","ZY":"{\\rm ZY}","Sr":"{\\rm S}","Ar":"{\\rm A}","Br":"{\\rm B}","Cr":"{\\rm C}","Ir":"{\\rm I}","Jr":"{\\rm J}","Prm":"{\\rm P}","X":"{\\rm X}","Y":"{\\rm Y}","SY":"{\\rm SY}","Pf":"{\\rm Pf}\\ts","Hf":"{\\rm Hf}\\ts","tr":"{\\rm tr}\\ts","End":"{\\rm{End}\\ts}","Hom":"{\\rm{Hom}}","sgn":"{\\rm sgn}\\ts","sign":"{\\rm sign}\\ts","qdet":"{\\rm qdet}\\ts","sdet":"{\\rm sdet}\\ts","Ber":"{\\rm Ber}\\ts","inv":"{\\rm inv}\\ts","inva":"{\\rm inv}","mi